  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Dustin, is the head of an Intelligence agency. He wants to send a secret message SSS to his colleague.The message is a single word consisting of only lowercase english letters but he decides to encrypt the message for security reasons. He makes a string MMM of length NNN, such that after deleting a substring of non-zero length from MMM, the remaining string is SSS.\n\nCalculate the number of all such possible strings he can form.\n\n###Input:\n\n\nFirst line will contain TTT, number of testcases. Then the testcases follow.\nFor each testcase the there is a single line which contains an integer, NNN and then a string SSS.\n###Output:\nFor each testcase, output the number of possible strings modulo 109+710^9+7109+7.\n\n###Constraints\n\n\n1≤T≤501 \\leq T \\leq 501≤T≤50\n1≤N≤10181 \\leq N \\leq 10^{18}1≤N≤1018\n1≤∣S∣≤1051 \\leq |S| \\leq 10^51≤∣S∣≤105\nSSS can contain only lowercase English letters.\n###Sample Input:\n2\n\n3 a\n\n3 ab\n\n###Sample Output:\n1326\n\n76",
